  "description": "Decision 266's kernel-code probe (phase3.1_export-island-padding item 2.1, decision 401: which texels Painter covers, every texel decided, and the infinite ring tap by tap) on the Tunic v10 low mesh, its texture set DefaultMaterial, kept in the UzmiGames asset repository and named by SHA-256 only (decision 099); document resolution 4096, the Tunic's Tier 1 size. User0-User7 added as RGB32F (a record whose template capture shows one of them not 32F is void); one fill with the eight channels active, Normal at opacity 1, default projection (read back), sources the authored float32 kernel code at the document size: User0-User2 one-hot the nine classes x mod 3 + 3 (y mod 3) of the texel (column x, row y from the top), User3 the UV ramp R = (x + 0.5)/N, G = (y + 0.5)/N, B = 0.5, User4 and User5 the periodic codes d and e (k/256, one 17 x 13 texel tile each), User6 (d + e)/2 and User7 1 - d. The eight maps at OpenEXR 32f with infinite padding and with passthrough (every covered texel must equal its source bit for bit, or the probe is void), every export step done twice in the session.",
